marie: fixed-cadence vsync and on-screen frame statistics

The vsync timer re-armed itself 16.7 ms after present() finished, so the
vsync notifications backboardd paces on slowed down by however long the
CPU copy into the panel took. Re-arm at absolute deadlines (skipping
missed ones) instead.

Once a second the framebuffer records vsyncs (v), frames shown (f),
swaps from backboardd (s), average/longest present() in ms (p) and the
busy percentage of each CPU (c), logs it (first minutes) and, with
boot-arg sweetfb_stats=1, draws it in the top-left corner of the panel.

